[37.104538, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;174m \u259d\u259d   \u259d\u259d \u001b[12G\u001b[38;5;246m~/dev/tend\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m\u276f \u001b[38;5;231mIn one codemode program: read the README of every station under examples/stations/brian/stations, have haiku sum each up in one line, put\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mthem in a new Claude Doc \"Stations at a glance\" as a plain markdown table, and start an Explore subagent to find which station has the \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mmost tests. Give me the link, then the subagent's answer when it lands.\u001b[39m                                                                   \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;246m\u23fa \u001b[39m\u001b[1mcodemode\u001b[22;39m\u001b[38;5;246m \u00b7 18 calls\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;81mconst\u001b[38;5;231m root = (\u001b[38;5;197mawait\u001b[38;5;231m \u001b[38;5;148mcwd\u001b[38;5;231m()) + \u001b[38;5;186m\"/examples/stations/brian/stations\"\u001b[38;5;231m;\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;81mconst\u001b[38;5;231m ls = \u001b[38;5;197mawait\u001b[38;5;231m tools.\u001b[38;5;148mBash\u001b[38;5;231m({ \u001b[38;5;148mcommand\u001b[38;5;231m: \u001b[38;5;186m`find \"\u001b[38;5;231m${root}\u001b[38;5;186m\" -minde"]
